%% v48 · 7 Jul 2026 · ★ VERSION DATA-SHAPE INVESTIGATED + LOCKED (Tina asked w/ Beef Lasagne screenshot + Kleftiko feta-pomegranate example: "do versions show the WHOLE instructions + the addition?"). CLONED live repo, read core.js applyRecipeVersion (L3094) + versionStripHTML (L3109) + real data (sp-lasagne, sp-tuna-pasta-bake in meals.js). FINDING = CURRENT ENGINE IS WHOLE-FIELD REPLACE, NOT MERGE: applyRecipeVersion overlays base with any of [feel·ingredients·method·costPP·time·nutrition·tip·storage·didYouKnow·goesWith·howThisFeels·cookTime·chefNotes·kcal·trivia·pairsWith] the version DEFINES; undefined fields fall through to base. ∴ TODAY each version = a FULL standalone recipe (tuna bake Creamy/Budget/Quick each RE-LIST all ingredients + RE-WRITE all steps). Cook taps chip → sees ONE complete recipe ✅ (matches screenshot). ANSWER to Tina: cook ALWAYS sees a whole woven recipe (RIGHT UX, keep it — Kleftiko source models it: twist folded INTO ingredient list + INTO step 4, NEVER a dangling "also add" footnote). Only question = how much YOU author. 🔒 DECISION — TWO VERSION MODES, ONE ENGINE: (A) STRUCTURAL (differ end-to-end: Classic/Budget/Quick) → KEEP full-field replace (correct, ~everything changes). (B) TWIST (base + small change: avocado-cilantro tzatziki · feta-pomegranate kleftiko · beetroot) → author a DELTA only; render MERGES base+delta into a full recipe. WHY B: full-rewrite per twist = ~5-10× typing + DRIFT (fix base later, copies don't inherit); delta = 3-6 lines + base fixes PROPAGATE + makes Code's twist-authoring RELIABLE (agent writes a small diff, physically can't silently drop a base ingredient). 🛠 MERGE-LAYER SPEC (small · additive · BACKWARDS-COMPAT — existing full-field versions byte-untouched): version may carry addIngredients[] · swapIngredients{from:to} · removeIngredients[] · insertSteps[{after:N,text}] · replaceStep{i,text} · appendSteps[]; applyRecipeVersion merges these ONLY WHEN full ingredients/method absent; optional "For this version" sublabel groups added items (Kleftiko "The Unusual Twists" pattern). ~30-40 lines core.js → belongs in SESSION-3 superset work. ★ FEEDS THE CLAUDE CODE BRIEF: twist versions = DELTA authoring contract (Code writes deltas not full recipes) = cheaper + safer for the tail. 🔜 NEXT: (1) BUILD the merge layer (banked · not pushed · node ✅ · Tina live-verifies + pushes) OR fold into Session-3; THEN (2) the Claude Code brief (moussaka=fields/method · tzatziki=versions/surprise · + the delta-version contract). ⬇ v47
